meta {
  name: Search a FHIR resource type: a searchset Bundle
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/fhir/:type
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~_count: 20
  ~_offset: 
  ~patient: Patient/12
  ~code: heart-rate
  ~gender: 
  ~birthdate: ge1980-01-01
  ~date: ge2025-06-01
  seed: 
  ~locale: 
}

params:path {
  type: Observation
}

docs {
  Synthetic, FHIR R4-shaped Patient, Observation, Condition and Encounter resources, invented by rules and seeded: see the data notes at the top of this tag. Search parameters for Patient: `_id`, `identifier`, `family`, `given`, `name`, `gender`, `birthdate`, `active`, plus `_count` (0 to 100, default 10), `_offset`, `seed` and `locale`. Token parameters take `code` or `system|code`, several separated by commas; dates take the prefixes `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `ge` and `le`; `patient` takes `12` or `Patient/12`. Any other parameter is a `400`. Search parameters for Observation: `_id`, `patient`, `subject`, `code`, `category`, `status`, `date`, plus `_count` (0 to 100, default 10), `_offset`, `seed` and `locale`. Token parameters take `code` or `system|code`, several separated by commas; dates take the prefixes `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `ge` and `le`; `patient` takes `12` or `Patient/12`. Any other parameter is a `400`. Search parameters for Condition: `_id`, `patient`, `subject`, `code`, `category`, `clinical-status`, `onset-date`, plus `_count` (0 to 100, default 10), `_offset`, `seed` and `locale`. Token parameters take `code` or `system|code`, several separated by commas; dates take the prefixes `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `ge` and `le`; `patient` takes `12` or `Patient/12`. Any other parameter is a `400`. Search parameters for Encounter: `_id`, `patient`, `subject`, `status`, `class`, `type`, `date`, plus `_count` (0 to 100, default 10), `_offset`, `seed` and `locale`. Token parameters take `code` or `system|code`, several separated by commas; dates take the prefixes `eq`, `ne`, `gt`, `lt`, `ge` and `le`; `patient` takes `12` or `Patient/12`. Any other parameter is a `400`.
}
